course: dictionary
lesson: 7884
title: Words that smell bad
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something smells or tastes. Rancid means gone off: food, especially fat, oil, butter, nuts or milk, has spoiled and now smells or tastes bad. «The seed coat smells like rancid butter.» That smell is a warning not to eat it.
explain: Rancid also has an informal meaning. If someone says «That joke was rancid», they mean it was horrible or very unpleasant, not that it had gone off. Ask yourself: is the thing a food, or is it an opinion or a joke? The context tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Look for the phrases «go rancid», «turn rancid» and «a rancid smell». Then swap in your meaning. If words like spoiled or horrible fit the sentence, you have found the right sense.
fact: Rancid means smelling or tasting bad because food has gone off.
fact: Fats and oils, such as butter and nuts, can turn rancid as they react with air over time.
fact: Informal use: «That joke was rancid» means the joke was horrible or very unpleasant.
fact: Useful phrases: «go rancid», «turn rancid», «a rancid smell».
fact: Context clue: if the thing is food, use the spoiled meaning; if it is a joke or an idea, use the slang meaning.
exercise: «The milk smelled sour and rancid, so Mum poured it away.» What does rancid mean here? | Fresh and cold | Very expensive | *Sweet and creamy | Gone off, smelling bad
exercise: Sam says, «That joke was rancid.» What does rancid mean? | Freshly baked | Full of nuts | Hot from the oven | *Horrible or very unpleasant
exercise: «The butter had turned rancid in the sun.» Find and copy the word that means gone off and smelling bad. | sun | turned | *rancid | butter
test: «The nuts had gone rancid, so we threw them out.» Why did they throw them out? | Because they smelled and tasted bad | Because they were too sweet | Because they were too big | *Because they had gone off and spoiled
test: Ella says the film was rancid. What does she mean? | It had gone off in the fridge | *It was horrible and very unpleasant | It was full of fresh fruit | It was very long
exam: «The seeds have a rancid smell, so nobody wants to eat them raw.» What does rancid tell you? | The seeds are brand new | The seeds are very cheap | *The seeds smell bad and have gone off | The seeds smell like flowers
